    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d865">

                <pb facs="0791" n="619" xml:id="pg619"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 703.5263</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-09T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 9, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>396. Your 328, February 5, 1 p.m. The Austro-Hungarian Government has severed
                    relations with the United States to-day, and Embassy at Vienna instructed by
                    Department to turn over American interests in Austria-Hungary to Spanish
                    Ambassador there. Also instructed to turn over British and Japanese interests to
                    Spanish Ambassador in accordance with arrangements which are understood to have
                    been made between governments concerned.</p>
                <p>Please inform Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
